WEBVTT

00:00.417 --> 00:02.585
You cowards!

00:03.461 --> 00:05.005
Just shut up...

00:05.088 --> 00:07.340
and place everything in me!

00:13.388 --> 00:15.181
What you need now

00:15.682 --> 00:18.518
is to be taught a lesson,
not be given a talking-to.

00:21.104 --> 00:22.731
I've made my decision.

00:23.857 --> 00:26.526
Eren was placed in
the Scout Regiment's custody

00:26.901 --> 00:29.696
in preparation for a scouting mission
beyond the wall.

02:07.585 --> 02:11.589
TROST DISTRICT

02:15.093 --> 02:18.680
OLD SCOUT REGIMENT HEADQUARTERS

02:18.763 --> 02:21.182
The old Scout Regiment headquarters...

02:22.976 --> 02:25.770
Just as you would expect
from a renovated old castle,

02:25.937 --> 02:28.523
it looks fancy and all.

02:29.566 --> 02:33.444
But being so far
from the wall and the river,

02:33.903 --> 02:36.656
it wound up being totally useless
for the Scout Regiment.

02:37.866 --> 02:41.744
That was back in the early days,
when everyone had high hopes.

02:42.537 --> 02:45.039
Still, to think that
this oversized decoration

02:45.123 --> 02:48.751
would end up as the perfect
holding place for you...

02:52.547 --> 02:54.465
Don't get cocky, rookie.

02:54.549 --> 02:55.383
Come again?

02:56.009 --> 02:58.094
I don't know if you're a Titan or what,

02:58.177 --> 03:02.599
but don't assume Captain Levi is going to
stick with a wet-behind-the-ears brat...

03:07.562 --> 03:10.690
Talking on a horse is a guaranteed way
to bite your tongue.

03:10.899 --> 03:14.944
First impressions are important.
I had that rookie scared stiff.

03:15.194 --> 03:18.448
Actually, I think he was shocked
at how dumb you are.

03:18.907 --> 03:22.327
Whatever the case,
it went exactly as planned.

03:22.827 --> 03:26.289
Hey. That's not how
you used to talk, you know.

03:27.290 --> 03:31.669
If, by any chance,
you're trying to imitate Captain Levi,

03:31.836 --> 03:33.421
could you cut it out?

03:33.755 --> 03:36.883
You're nothing like him at all, actually.

03:38.301 --> 03:40.595
Are you trying to nag me, Petra?

03:40.929 --> 03:44.807
If you want to act like you're my wife,
there's more you need to do first.

03:45.642 --> 03:47.977
I wish you had bitten
your tongue off and died.

03:48.394 --> 03:51.022
Bragging all about
how many Titans you've killed...

03:51.231 --> 03:52.482
Don't worry.

03:52.982 --> 03:55.777
I bragged about you too,
while I was at it.

03:57.362 --> 04:01.199
They're the members of Scout Regiment's
Special Operations Squad,

04:01.741 --> 04:03.326
also known as "Squad Levi."

04:03.534 --> 04:05.161
Sheesh, you're disgraceful!

04:05.912 --> 04:06.913
Petra Rall,

04:07.163 --> 04:11.125
with 10 Titan kills, and 48 kill-assists.

04:12.585 --> 04:17.131
Oruo Bozad, 39 kills and 9 assists.

04:18.007 --> 04:19.550
They're as elite as they come.

04:22.387 --> 04:26.724
Eld Gin, 14 kills, 32 assists.

04:27.642 --> 04:31.980
Gunther Schultz, 7 kills, 40 assists.

04:33.606 --> 04:37.860
Each is an accomplished Scout
personally handpicked by Captain Levi.

04:38.361 --> 04:39.279
And...

04:40.488 --> 04:45.118
they're the people who will end up
killing me if I ever go out of control.

04:47.161 --> 04:48.788
There are weeds everywhere.

04:49.539 --> 04:50.915
The place has really gone to hell...

04:51.124 --> 04:53.334
It hasn't been used in a long time.

04:53.626 --> 04:55.336
I bet it's pretty dusty on the inside too.

04:55.712 --> 04:58.506
That's a serious problem.

04:59.716 --> 05:01.634
Let's get to work at once.

05:10.727 --> 05:12.979
I've finished cleaning upstairs.

05:14.772 --> 05:17.400
Where am I to sleep in this facility, sir?

05:18.985 --> 05:20.820
Your room's in the basement.

05:21.362 --> 05:23.656
The basement again?

05:23.740 --> 05:24.866
Of course.

05:25.408 --> 05:27.827
You don't have full control of yourself.

05:28.953 --> 05:30.705
Should you turn
into a Titan in your sleep,

05:30.788 --> 05:33.124
we can keep you restrained
right there in the basement.

05:33.708 --> 05:38.004
That was one of the conditions
I was given when I took custody of you.

05:38.504 --> 05:39.922
It's a rule we have to follow.

05:42.800 --> 05:43.926
I'll go check your work.

05:44.385 --> 05:46.471
You take over here, Eren.

05:46.721 --> 05:47.555
Yes, sir.

05:53.519 --> 05:55.521
You look disappointed, Eren.

05:55.772 --> 05:56.606
What?

05:56.689 --> 06:00.693
Oh, I hope you don't mind if I call you
"Eren" like Captain Levi does.

06:01.277 --> 06:03.154
He sets the rules here.

06:03.905 --> 06:04.739
I see.

06:04.906 --> 06:09.452
I don't mind, but did I really
look disappointed just now?

06:09.786 --> 06:11.412
It's not an unusual reaction.

06:11.996 --> 06:15.750
He's not quite the great, perfect hero
society makes him out to be, is he?

06:16.250 --> 06:20.505
The real Captain Levi
is shorter than you would expect,

06:20.755 --> 06:23.174
temperamental, crude, and unsociable.

06:24.467 --> 06:27.095
No, what surprises me is how serious he is

06:27.428 --> 06:30.348
about adhering to
the higher-ups' arrangement.

06:30.890 --> 06:32.642
You thought that,
because he's strong and skilled,

06:32.725 --> 06:35.311
he didn't have to follow
the rules like everyone else?

06:35.895 --> 06:36.729
Right.

06:37.522 --> 06:40.191
I thought that he didn't take orders
from anyone...

06:40.775 --> 06:42.777
I don't really know the details myself,

06:43.236 --> 06:46.072
but I think he might've been
like that at one time.

06:47.406 --> 06:50.201
They say before he joined the Scouts,

06:50.409 --> 06:53.329
Captain Levi was an infamous rogue
in the capital's underground market.

06:54.831 --> 06:56.749
So how did he...

06:57.333 --> 06:58.251
Beats me.

06:58.751 --> 07:00.503
I don't know what happened,

07:01.003 --> 07:03.131
but I hear he wound up
being dragged into the Scouts

07:03.214 --> 07:05.716
after giving in to Commander Erwin.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.094
The commander?

07:09.178 --> 07:10.263
Hey, Eren!

07:10.346 --> 07:11.514
Yes?

07:12.348 --> 07:13.850
This is completely unacceptable.

07:14.016 --> 07:15.685
Do it all over again.

07:18.521 --> 07:19.730
An expedition 30 days from now

07:19.814 --> 07:22.400
to establish a logistic base
outside the wall...

07:23.359 --> 07:26.529
and newly-graduated rookies
will be participating too?

07:27.113 --> 07:29.031
Assuming any rookies do join us.

07:30.783 --> 07:34.620
Whatever the case, this all seems
a bit too hasty if you ask me.

07:35.496 --> 07:38.833
Eren's current treatment
is only temporary.

07:39.167 --> 07:42.503
We need to show the Royal Government
as quickly as possible

07:42.587 --> 07:44.589
that his existence is
beneficial for humankind.

07:45.715 --> 07:49.218
Otherwise, the Military Police,
or someone else, will interfere again--

07:49.302 --> 07:52.221
Are you using rhetoric on me too, Erwin?

07:58.186 --> 08:00.730
I see your nose is
as sharp as ever, Miche.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.692
Not as sharp as yours, though.

08:06.235 --> 08:07.737
I'll fill you in when the time is right.

08:15.953 --> 08:19.582
I assume our orders to remain on standby
will last for a few more days,

08:19.957 --> 08:22.335
but I hear they're planning
a major expedition beyond the wall

08:22.418 --> 08:23.878
30 days from now,

08:24.587 --> 08:28.382
and that fresh graduates are going
to participate right off the bat too.

08:28.758 --> 08:30.426
Is that true, Eld?

08:30.635 --> 08:32.303
That seems pretty sudden to me,

08:33.012 --> 08:37.558
especially since the rookies already
had to endure this latest Titan attack.

08:38.309 --> 08:41.103
I bet those brats
were scared out of their wits.

08:41.437 --> 08:42.855
Is this true, sir?

08:42.939 --> 08:46.025
I'm not in charge of
coming up with missions.

08:46.651 --> 08:48.486
But, knowing Erwin,

08:48.736 --> 08:51.280
he has put far more thought into this
than we have.

08:51.739 --> 08:55.326
Indeed, there has never been
a situation like this before.

08:55.826 --> 08:59.497
So many lives were lost establishing
a route to reclaim Wall Maria.

08:59.580 --> 09:01.749
Just when it seemed
like it went up in smoke,

09:01.832 --> 09:05.336
a completely different form of hope
suddenly presented itself.

09:13.844 --> 09:15.846
It's still hard to believe,

09:16.389 --> 09:20.101
but how does this "changing into a Titan"
thing work anyway, Eren?

09:21.185 --> 09:24.230
My memories of it aren't very clear,

09:24.981 --> 09:26.607
but it's like being in a trance...

09:27.358 --> 09:30.361
I set it off by inflicting
self-harm, though.

09:30.778 --> 09:32.113
I take my hand like so and...

09:32.780 --> 09:33.698
What?

09:33.781 --> 09:37.076
Come to think of it,
why is this the only thing I know?

09:38.286 --> 09:40.079
You guys know you can't get
any more out of him

09:40.496 --> 09:42.665
than what's in the reports.

09:44.250 --> 09:46.252
Not that she won't try, of course.

09:48.796 --> 09:52.174
Better hope you don't end up dead
when she tinkers with you...

09:52.717 --> 09:55.261
- Eren.
- Who is "she"?

10:00.433 --> 10:03.644
Good evening, members of Squad Levi!

10:04.437 --> 10:06.439
How is castle life treating you?

10:06.731 --> 10:07.857
You're early.

10:08.107 --> 10:10.401
I just couldn't help myself!

10:10.651 --> 10:12.153
Section Commander Hange...

10:12.361 --> 10:13.654
Sorry for the wait, Eren!

10:14.488 --> 10:19.660
I'm actually in charge of examining
two Titans we caught in town.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.830
I would like you to help
with my experiments tomorrow,

10:23.205 --> 10:24.832
so I came to get your permission.

10:25.458 --> 10:27.209
Experiments?

10:28.127 --> 10:30.129
- What would I have to do?
- Why...

10:30.880 --> 10:33.758
The most exhilarating thing of all,
of course!

10:34.300 --> 10:38.012
But I'm not in a position
to give permission myself.

10:38.929 --> 10:41.974
I don't have authority
over myself, you see...

10:42.058 --> 10:44.226
Levi! What are Eren's plans for tomorrow?

10:45.019 --> 10:46.187
Cleaning the garden.

10:46.270 --> 10:48.522
Great! It's decided!

10:50.650 --> 10:52.568
Eren! I look forward to tomorrow!

10:52.985 --> 10:54.612
Yes, right.

10:55.655 --> 10:58.824
But what kind of Titan experiments
are we talking about here?

11:01.035 --> 11:03.704
As I said,
what kind of experiments are we--

11:03.788 --> 11:05.373
Hey, stop! Don't ask that!

11:05.915 --> 11:08.376
Oh, I knew it...

11:08.959 --> 11:11.921
I thought you might
be curious enough to ask...

11:23.391 --> 11:25.393
You want to know that badly, do you?

11:25.768 --> 11:27.353
Well, if you insist,

11:28.145 --> 11:30.439
then I guess I better tell you all about

11:31.273 --> 11:35.111
the little ones we recently caught...

11:37.238 --> 11:40.032
I began by repeating the same experiment

11:40.366 --> 11:42.368
that we've conducted
during five previous captures.

11:45.162 --> 11:46.080
Hello!

11:49.125 --> 11:52.211
First was an attempt at communication.

11:53.129 --> 11:54.213
How are you feeling?

11:54.880 --> 11:55.798
What's your name?

11:56.090 --> 11:57.258
Are you in pain?

11:58.217 --> 12:00.010
Section Commander! You're too close!

12:02.680 --> 12:03.681
Hello!

12:04.557 --> 12:05.683
Nice weather, isn't it?

12:05.891 --> 12:06.892
Are you hungry?

12:08.978 --> 12:10.813
Whoa, that was close!

12:10.896 --> 12:12.356
That's dangerous, Section Commander!

12:12.857 --> 12:14.108
Unfortunately, I had to conclude

12:14.358 --> 12:18.696
that there's no hope of communicating
with these ones either.

12:21.198 --> 12:23.993
However, my time spent
interacting with the Titans

12:24.368 --> 12:28.497
was fulfilling enough to
make me forget my daily exhaustion.

12:29.957 --> 12:34.795
Once upon a time,
there existed a clan that ate humans.

12:36.297 --> 12:40.259
And I don't mean you Titans.
I'm talking about a clan of people.

12:41.093 --> 12:44.388
They would hide in caves on mountainsides

12:44.930 --> 12:47.558
and attack any travelers who passed by.

12:47.641 --> 12:51.854
They would steal their valuables,
kill them, and eat their flesh.

12:52.897 --> 12:56.192
Here we go again.
Another one of her naming ceremonies.

12:56.275 --> 12:58.986
Yes. What did she call
the last ones again?

12:59.069 --> 13:01.030
"Chikatiloni" and "Albert."

13:01.238 --> 13:06.327
Ultimately,
they kept this up for 25 years,

13:06.785 --> 13:10.873
during which they supposedly
preyed on over 500 people.

13:12.041 --> 13:15.836
Probably more humans
than you've eaten, in fact.

13:16.962 --> 13:20.633
They also tried eating them
in all sorts of ways.

13:21.300 --> 13:23.052
Making steaks out of rump meat,

13:23.969 --> 13:26.722
dicing up leg meat and
adding it to a stew,

13:27.223 --> 13:30.476
grinding tough meat
into patties and frying it,

13:30.893 --> 13:34.438
making sausages
from blood clots and innards...

13:34.939 --> 13:38.817
Indeed, they possessed
the concept of cooking!

13:39.109 --> 13:41.362
That's where they differ from you.

13:42.279 --> 13:46.617
However, this clan of cannibals
was caught and executed

13:46.700 --> 13:48.285
after making a single mistake.

13:49.036 --> 13:51.205
That's where you're just like them.

13:51.664 --> 13:55.209
You guys made the mistake
of attacking humankind

13:55.292 --> 13:57.002
and wound up getting caught.

13:58.587 --> 14:01.006
So I'm going to name you two

14:01.090 --> 14:04.510
after the man who was
the leader of this clan.

14:05.261 --> 14:06.512
You're "Sawney."

14:07.263 --> 14:08.889
You're "Beane."

14:10.599 --> 14:11.767
But don't worry.

14:12.268 --> 14:15.145
I'm not going to execute you.

14:16.063 --> 14:17.314
Nice to meet you, Sawney.

14:17.982 --> 14:19.275
And you too, Beane.

14:20.734 --> 14:22.278
Let's all be friends!

14:24.113 --> 14:26.532
And that's how I named
the seven-meter Titan "Beane"

14:26.991 --> 14:30.411
and the four-meter Titan "Sawney."

14:35.332 --> 14:38.460
Next, I tested blocking them
from sunlight.

14:39.211 --> 14:42.214
From the fact that Titans become
less active as the night progresses,

14:42.298 --> 14:47.303
this experiment corroborates that
they somehow use sunlight for energy.

14:48.470 --> 14:51.599
It was from this that I found
a substantial difference between the two.

14:52.474 --> 14:55.227
Yes. You did great, Sawney.

14:56.228 --> 14:58.606
Goodnight. I'll see you tomorrow.

14:59.732 --> 15:04.445
While Sawney became sluggish
after only one hour out of sunlight...

15:05.154 --> 15:08.699
You sure love to stay up late,
don't you, Beane?

15:09.408 --> 15:12.494
Okay, then, I'll hang out with you
as long as you like.

15:13.871 --> 15:16.665
...Beane was still his energetic self
three hours later.

15:20.210 --> 15:22.296
It came as another shock to me.

15:22.630 --> 15:24.924
They don't require food or water,

15:25.007 --> 15:28.177
and even though they have vocal organs,
they don't need to breathe.

15:28.761 --> 15:31.972
The only thing they need is sunlight.

15:32.890 --> 15:35.309
I'm curious to know what happens
after prolonged sunlight deprivation,

15:35.559 --> 15:38.520
but I can't risk having them die,
you know?

15:39.647 --> 15:43.233
We've accidentally killed
the previous ones that we've caught.

15:44.193 --> 15:45.903
We tried decapitating some
as an experiment

15:45.986 --> 15:48.030
but accidentally cut
the napes of their necks too.

15:48.739 --> 15:52.034
Their names were Chikatiloni and Albert.

15:52.868 --> 15:54.912
They had such cute smiles.

15:55.913 --> 15:59.083
I did something truly terrible to them.

16:01.251 --> 16:04.296
I never want that to happen again.

16:06.340 --> 16:07.967
Ms. Hange...

16:10.636 --> 16:11.595
After that,

16:11.679 --> 16:14.765
the next step was
physical contact with the Titans!

16:15.015 --> 16:17.893
I tested to see if they felt pain!

16:24.483 --> 16:26.860
Section Commander!
There's no need for you to scream!

16:26.944 --> 16:28.904
I can't do this and not scream!

16:29.279 --> 16:32.324
Beane is in so much pain!

16:32.950 --> 16:34.910
Beane! Hang in there!

16:34.994 --> 16:36.787
Stay strong!

16:38.539 --> 16:41.250
I needed to determine
if Titans have any other weaknesses

16:41.500 --> 16:43.460
besides their napes, you see.

16:44.795 --> 16:46.797
It was an agonizing task.

16:49.216 --> 16:50.134
Sawney...

16:50.759 --> 16:53.220
Hey, I've stabbed you in the heart.

16:53.554 --> 16:56.390
Does it not hurt? How does it feel?

16:57.641 --> 17:00.894
Compared to Beane,
Sawney seemed more introverted

17:01.478 --> 17:03.522
and didn't respond much at all.

17:04.773 --> 17:06.650
What?

17:06.734 --> 17:07.818
What is it?

17:10.904 --> 17:12.865
Section Commander! Please step back!

17:14.783 --> 17:18.412
- Almost got me that time, Sawney!
- You're seriously going to die!

17:20.289 --> 17:24.043
So Sawney's not very good
at expressing himself.

17:24.585 --> 17:27.004
He just keeps trying to chomp my head off.

17:27.087 --> 17:28.797
Ms. Hange.

17:30.507 --> 17:35.095
How can you be so lighthearted
when dealing with Titans?

17:37.639 --> 17:38.557
I mean...

17:39.224 --> 17:40.893
They're our natural enemy,

17:40.976 --> 17:43.395
and they've driven humanity
to the verge of extinction.

17:44.146 --> 17:48.442
Surely, you've experienced the threat
they pose countless times yourself.

17:49.860 --> 17:50.778
I have.

17:51.278 --> 17:54.031
I've watched Titans
kill friend after friend

17:54.114 --> 17:55.449
right before my very eyes.

17:56.867 --> 18:01.747
When I first joined the Scouts,
I fought the Titans out of hate.

18:02.831 --> 18:05.834
But, one day, I made a realization...

18:07.252 --> 18:11.006
after I kicked the severed head
of a three-meter-tall Titan.

18:12.633 --> 18:14.927
It was light. Unusually light.

18:15.803 --> 18:17.429
The Titan's body, I mean.

18:19.556 --> 18:23.560
When you think about it,
it shouldn't even be possible

18:23.644 --> 18:26.063
for such large creatures
to stand and walk on two legs.

18:26.980 --> 18:28.649
Every Titan was the same.

18:29.274 --> 18:34.363
Severed limbs weren't nearly
as heavy as they should have been.

18:35.239 --> 18:37.199
And when you transformed,

18:37.282 --> 18:41.161
I was told your Titan body
appeared out of nowhere.

18:43.288 --> 18:44.790
It's my belief

18:45.624 --> 18:51.797
that how they appear to us
is nothing like what they really are.

18:56.593 --> 18:59.596
For decades,
we've tried an offensive approach

18:59.888 --> 19:01.807
that feeds off of hate.

19:02.891 --> 19:05.686
I want to try to view the Titans

19:05.936 --> 19:07.771
from an angle
different from the existing one.

19:08.856 --> 19:11.108
It might end as a waste of time,

19:11.775 --> 19:14.820
but I'm going to do it.

19:22.578 --> 19:26.123
Joining the Scouts has been
nothing but surprise after surprise.

19:27.082 --> 19:30.252
It's not just Ms. Hange.
Everyone is strange.

19:31.211 --> 19:34.047
It's practically a haven of oddballs.

19:34.798 --> 19:35.716
Still...

19:36.592 --> 19:38.927
A group of people that seek change...

19:39.428 --> 19:41.388
That's what the Scouts are all about!

19:42.806 --> 19:43.807
Ms. Hange!

19:45.017 --> 19:49.146
Would you mind telling me
even more about your experiments?

19:49.438 --> 19:51.023
Are you sure?

19:51.106 --> 19:51.940
Yes!

19:52.024 --> 19:53.942
I think it would be good
to know as much as possible

19:54.026 --> 19:56.236
before tomorrow's experiments!

19:57.070 --> 19:58.739
Good point.

19:59.323 --> 20:02.993
Yes. I did gloss over
a lot of things just now.

20:03.285 --> 20:05.329
I should go into further detail!

20:05.579 --> 20:07.873
- This could take a while...
- That's okay!

20:08.207 --> 20:13.378
I'll start off with the hypothesis I had
the first time we caught a Titan!

20:16.256 --> 20:20.969
As such, that experiment
provided no new information!

20:21.678 --> 20:25.432
I'm sure they teach everyone
this stuff during cadet training.

20:25.682 --> 20:27.100
You knew all this, right?

20:27.809 --> 20:30.354
Yes, I already knew it all.

20:30.854 --> 20:33.232
So now I'll explain things further

20:33.315 --> 20:35.859
by going over everything again
with my own theories!

20:35.943 --> 20:36.777
What?

20:37.110 --> 20:37.986
I'm...

20:38.070 --> 20:39.404
First is how Titans...

20:40.197 --> 20:41.657
Is Section Commander Hange here?

20:42.616 --> 20:43.617
The test subjects...

20:44.243 --> 20:46.411
Both of the Titans have been killed!

20:56.546 --> 20:59.091
Sawney! Beane!

20:59.508 --> 21:00.634
No way...

21:01.218 --> 21:03.095
Tell me this isn't happening!

21:05.055 --> 21:06.765
They were such valuable test subjects.

21:07.391 --> 21:08.600
Did soldiers do this?

21:08.809 --> 21:11.520
Yes. They haven't found
who was responsible yet.

21:12.187 --> 21:14.523
Apparently, both were killed
at the same time just before dawn.

21:14.940 --> 21:18.777
By the time the guards noticed,
whoever did it had used ODM to get away.

21:19.236 --> 21:22.155
So a team of at least
two people planned this, right?

21:22.823 --> 21:24.366
Sawney!

21:24.449 --> 21:25.367
Just look.

21:25.784 --> 21:28.161
Section Commander Hange is raving mad.

21:30.414 --> 21:32.416
How did this happen...

21:32.791 --> 21:35.711
Let's go.
The rest is the Military Police's job.

21:36.378 --> 21:37.421
Yes, sir...

21:40.966 --> 21:42.551
What do you see here?

21:45.387 --> 21:46.888
What do you think the enemy is?

21:47.973 --> 21:48.890
What?

21:51.768 --> 21:54.604
Sorry. That was a strange thing to ask.

23:42.838 --> 23:47.175
As the hunt for Sawney and Beane's
killers gets underway,

23:47.467 --> 23:50.595
Mikasa, Armin, and the members
of the 104th Cadet Corps Class,

23:50.846 --> 23:55.684
with hopes and dreams of their own,
must decide which regiment to join.
